1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:03,756
Part eighteen. Getting more from every list.

2
00:00:04,610 --> 00:00:11,140
Every list has a search box: type a name, phone number, city or document number.

3
00:00:11,140 --> 00:00:13,997
Tap a column heading to sort by it.

4
00:00:14,890 --> 00:00:18,102
The filter button has ready-made filters,

5
00:00:18,102 --> 00:00:22,959
like follow-up overdue or up to 3 kilowatts for PM Surya Ghar.

6
00:00:22,959 --> 00:00:28,521
You can add your own filter, group the list, and save it as a favorite.

7
00:00:29,410 --> 00:00:36,712
Change how you see the list: board by stage, calendar by date, pivot table, graph,

8
00:00:36,712 --> 00:00:37,336
or map.

9
00:00:37,336 --> 00:00:40,631
The same filters apply in every view.

10
00:00:41,530 --> 00:00:45,523
Export saves the list as Excel, PDF or CSV.

11
00:00:45,523 --> 00:00:52,579
Import CSV brings in many records at once from Excel: it adds the good rows,

12
00:00:52,579 --> 00:00:56,108
skips duplicates and lists any errors.

13
00:00:57,260 --> 00:01:00,826
Next video: Dashboard, reports and alerts.

